Screenshots are OFF for the duration of Phase 7 (the Verse AI layer).

WHY

`npm run verify` runs the screenshot suite last, and the full gate now exceeds
the ten-minute cap on a single tool invocation. What happens then is not a
slow gate — it is a gate that gets BACKGROUNDED to fit, and a hook running in
the background has stopped gating anything. The commit lands while Playwright
is still opening a browser.

So the choice is not "fast gate vs. thorough gate". It is "a gate that blocks
the commit vs. a gate that watches it go past". Typecheck, lint, build and the
whole vitest suite still run on every commit and still refuse it.

WHAT THIS DOES NOT COVER

Everything the conventions skill says about rendered pages is still true, and
none of it is suspended:

  - six UI commits once shipped with the suite green and no page ever opened;
  - `materialiseRecipient` never called `advanceConversation`, and typecheck,
    lint and the entire db suite passed — only the picture showed sixteen
    threads sorting above real customers;
  - a Tailwind size key silently overriding a spacing key of the same name is
    invisible to every source-level check.

Skipping the suite per commit does not make those safe. It defers them, which
is only acceptable because the deferral has a fixed end.

UNTIL WHEN

The tag. `npm run test:visual` runs in full before Phase 7 is tagged, with the
new baselines reviewed as images rather than accepted as passing — the
knowledge base with an indexed document and a failed one, the campaign wizard,
a running campaign, a thread Verse answered from the knowledge base, and a
thread it handed off.

DELETE THIS FILE at that point. It is a file rather than an edit to the hook
so that the state is in `git status`, in the diff of the commit that set it,
and is undone by deleting something rather than by remembering to restore a
line somebody changed.
